<title>BELGIUM: EU details first 1997/98 sugar output forecast.</title>
<headline>EU details first 1997/98 sugar output forecast.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union sugar production was expected to fall to 16.37 million tonnes in 1997/98 (July/June), from 16.84 million tonnes in 1996/97, the European Commission said in a preliminary forecast on Wednesday.</p>
<p>		 EU sugar production (million tonnes):</p>
<p>				   1997/98	     1996/97</p>
<p> 1.  Area (million/ha)	2.043		     2.020</p>
<p> 2.  White Sugar</p>
<p>     Yield (t/ha)	 7.86			8.18</p>
<p> 3.  Beet output	 16.055		    16.515</p>
<p>     Cane output	  0.270		     0.275</p>
<p>     Molasses output    0.044		     0.047</p>
<p>     Total output	16.369		    16.837</p>
<p> 4.  Carryover from</p>
<p>     previous season    0.917		     0.685</p>
<p> 5.  Total supplies</p>
<p>     (3+4)		 17.286		    17.522</p>
<p> 6.  Of which</p>
<p>     &quot;A&quot; Quota	   11.777		    11.717</p>
<p>     &quot;B&quot; Quota	    2.556		     2.450</p>
<p>     &quot;C&quot; Non-quota	2.953		     3.355</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>Carry forward</p>
<p>     to next season     1.000		     0.917</p>
<p>     Exports		1.953		     2.438</p>
<p> 7.  Consumption	 12.600		    12.600</p>
<p>-Peter Blackburn Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
